## Why

The API is on Express **4.22.2** (`package.json` range `^4.21.2`) with `@types/express` `^4.17.21`. Current Express 5 is **5.3.0**; current `@types/express` 5 is **5.0.6**.

T0380 and T0381 already landed the two code breaks that had to ship while still on Express 4:

- Query sanitizer replaces `req.query` with `Object.defineProperty` (`src/middleware/sanitizeIncomingStrings.ts`) and tests the getter case.
- `beginAfterListen` exits on a listen error before background jobs (`src/lib/listenStartup.ts`, wired from `src/index.ts`).

This task is the package and types bump, plus the remaining checks from the task description.

## Target

- `express@5` → `^5.3.0` (5.3.0, the current 5.x release)
- `@types/express@5` → `^5.0.6`
- Leave the existing `qs` override (`^6.16.0`); Express 5.3 already pulls a patched `qs`.

`scripts/package_upgrade.sh` is an untracked stub that feeds `npm list` into `npm install --save-dev`. Replace it with the commands for this upgrade: install those two packages at the versions above, then `npm test`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run build:all`. Commit the script on the feature branch. Do not commit the other dirty files already on `main` (`UPGRADES.md` local edit, moved plan files, `docs/design/*`, `scripts/enable-pgvector.sh`).

## Change

1. **Install** Express 5.3 and `@types/express` 5. Run `tsc` and fix compile errors. Expect stricter handler, `params`, and `query` typing. Keep fixes mechanical (narrow a param, adjust a callback signature). If a type error needs a behavior change, stop and call it out before expanding scope.
2. **`req.body` when no body is sent.** Express 5 leaves `req.body` `undefined` instead of `{}`. Audit routes that `parse(req.body)` against client calls that POST or DELETE with no body. Where a handler should accept that, use `parse(req.body ?? {})`. Do not blanket-wrap every parse.
3. **`res.sendFile` and hidden folders.** Upload download (`src/routes/v1/uploads.ts`) and the production SPA fallback (`src/index.ts`) pass absolute paths. Express 5 `send` 404s `dotfiles: "ignore"` when any path segment is hidden (a directory starting with `.`). Default `UPLOAD_DIR` (`data/uploads`) and a normal client `dist/` are fine. Add a short note in `INSTALL.md` (next to `UPLOAD_DIR`) and `UPGRADES.md`: an `UPLOAD_DIR` under a hidden directory (for example `/home/user/.taskmesh/uploads`) will 404 downloads. Apply that note without taking the unrelated uncommitted `UPGRADES.md` edits.
4. **5.1–5.3 skim (no code unless a check fails):**
   - 5.1: `Uint8Array` in `res.send`, `res.sendFile` `etag` option, `res.links` — unused.
   - 5.2.0 / 5.2.1: extended query-parser change was reverted. `res.redirect(undefined)` warns; existing redirects use `res.redirect(302, url)`. `urlencoded` stays `extended: false`.
   - 5.3: `res.send` omits `Content-Length` when `Transfer-Encoding` is set (we do not set it). QUERY can 304 (we do not route QUERY). Invalid `body-parser` `limit` now throws; `"10mb"` and `"1mb"` stay valid. `content-disposition` 2 no longer quotes token filenames from `res.download` / `res.attachment` / `res.sendFile`. Our downloads set `Content-Disposition` themselves, with quotes. Confirm `sendFile` does not replace that header. Update a test only if one asserts the exact header from Express.

## Tests and checks

- Existing sanitizer and listen-startup tests stay green under Express 5.
- Add or extend a test only if the body audit finds a handler that must tolerate a missing body.
- `npm test`, `npm run lint`, `npm run build:all`.
- Smoke on the DEV API (`:3001`): login, one upload download, and a JSON route that reads `req.query` after the sanitizer. Production SPA deep-link (`sendFile` of `index.html`) needs a production build; hit that route if `client/dist` is present, and say so in the QA checklist if it is not.

